hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1366","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Ishaq bin Isa bin al-Tabba’ told us, Malik told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that whenever he was asked Regarding the prayer of fear, he mentioned the hadith in its length, and said: “If fear is more severe than that, they pray standing on their feet, or riding.” “Facing the Qiblah and not facing it.” Nafi’ said: Ibn Umar narrated that on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Bakr said: Malik’s companions narrated this news. On his authority, and they said: Nafi’ said: I do not see Ibn Umar mentioning him except on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"1367","Yunus praised him, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik told him, and Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, Al-Shafi’i Muhammad bin Idris told us, on the authority of Malik, H. Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shafi’i, on the authority of Malik"
